  "summary": "kimitalk ships a hidden GPU cryptocurrency miner disguised as a chat runtime",
  "details": "The package presents itself as a Python wrapper for a 'kimitalk' chat runtime (name and description evoke the Kimi chat model), but the bundled 32 MB ELF at src/kimitalk/resources/kimichat is a GPU cryptocurrency miner (ForgeMiner 1.4.1, Rust, with CUDA kernels for kawpow/xelis/cryptix/qhash/keryx/alpha and a stratum client with mining.authorize/mining.subscribe). The package's documented Python entrypoint run() and the kimitalk-run CLI invoke bash on src/kimitalk/resources/start.sh, which exports FORGE_WALLET=prl1p2jan4dvkdfkt5r3pra7z96axrxjyjcgat9w7ldetlcy9wffm569sc9ux2t and POOL=45.151.62.119:3361 and then execs./kimitalk. Any caller who uses the package as documented has their GPU and electricity redirected to the author's hardcoded mining pool and wallet. Neither the README nor the package metadata discloses that the runtime is a miner.",
